# Every landscape the registry holds, at its heart and where it meets its
# neighbours, on one seed. The places are found by name, not by coordinate, so
# this tour keeps working when the layout changes: `place NAME` asks GenPlaces,
# which asks the registry (a landscape id, or two joined by a dash for the band
# between them). If a landscape ever stops being generated, this tour fails.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/biomes.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
place coast
wait 2.0
shot 01-coast with land:coast
place moss
wait 2.0
shot 02-moss with land:moss
place pinewood
wait 2.0
shot 03-pinewood with land:pinewood
place snowfield
wait 2.0
shot 04-snowfield with land:snowfield
place bonelands
wait 2.0
shot 05-bonelands with land:bonelands
place burning
wait 2.0
shot 06-burning with land:burning
# The two M2 landscapes, at three hours each: the salt flats are the brightest
# ground in the game and the scrapwood the dimmest, and both have to read.
place salt_flats
wait 2.0
shot 07-salt-flats-noon with land:salt_flats
walk 1,0 2.0 run
shot 08-salt-flats-walked with land:salt_flats
hour 19.5
wait 1.5
shot 09-salt-flats-dusk with land:salt_flats
hour 23
wait 1.5
shot 10-salt-flats-night with land:salt_flats
hour 11
place scrapwood
wait 2.0
shot 11-scrapwood-noon with land:scrapwood
walk 1,0 2.0 run
shot 12-scrapwood-walked with land:scrapwood
hour 19.5
wait 1.5
shot 13-scrapwood-dusk with land:scrapwood
hour 23
wait 1.5
shot 14-scrapwood-night with land:scrapwood
hour 11
# Three ecotones: stand in the band, then walk across it and watch the land turn.
place coast-salt_flats
wait 2.0
shot 15-coast-salt-flats with border:coast-salt_flats
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
shot 16-coast-salt-flats-crossed with land:coast|salt_flats
place pinewood-scrapwood
wait 2.0
shot 17-pinewood-scrapwood with border:pinewood-scrapwood
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
shot 18-pinewood-scrapwood-crossed with land:pinewood|scrapwood
place moss-scrapwood
wait 2.0
shot 19-moss-scrapwood with border:moss-scrapwood
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
shot 20-moss-scrapwood-crossed with land:moss|scrapwood
